# Zone 1, room 10 (grey box): Crouch-dash under. BUILD.md s5 tech 10, "crouch, then dash, keeps
# the 28-tall hitbox. Taught by a low gap"; docs/adr/0010 (Crouch, Crouch-dash, Low gaps),
# docs/adr/0014 (doors). Grey boxes, not art.
#
# Layout (units; a tile is 32): 60 x 34 tiles. The floor's top is y 960 (row 30). The hall is 576
# tall (rows 12..29) under a solid ceiling, so a wall that stands from floor to ceiling has no way
# over it. Two doors, 128 tall, on the floor: west and east at y 832..960; the player arrives at
# x 74.
#   A  x 448..512   a wall 64 thick with a gap in its bottom row: 32 tall, 64 long. The safe first
#                   encounter: floor both sides, nothing that hurts, a dash started anywhere from
#                   the west door on crosses it.
#   B  x 960..1088  the same wall 128 thick (the gap 32 tall, 128 long). The real one.
#      x 1088..1216 a landing, then x 1216..1376 a pit (5 tiles of '~', a hazard), then floor to
#                   the east door. A plain run-jump clears the pit with margin (about 190 u of
#                   reach).
# The numbers that matter: the standing body is 44 tall, the crouched one 28, a gap is 32. A
# crouch-dash is 180 u in 9 frames plus 3 carry frames at 10 u, so 210 u and a short slide; the
# crouched body cannot move, so a dash that ends inside a gap strands the player until the 24
# frame ground cooldown allows a second one (ADR-0010 level rule: a crouch-only gap is at most one
# crouch-dash long; B is 128). From the face (x 950) the dash leaves B with the body standing at
# about 1100; started within about 80 u of the face it still gets out, started further back (860
# and less) it ends inside and needs the second dash.
#
# Why the tech is needed. The gaps are too low to walk (44 > 32), a standing dash stops at the
# face (x 950 for B), a hop in a low gap never crawls (the crouched box cannot move, in the air
# either), and nothing goes over or under: both walls run from the floor to the solid ceiling and
# the floor below is solid. Ash can crouch before this room (the stick down) and has been taught
# every tech up to 9; this is the first place that needs the crouch-dash.
# Not the only way, and why it still is the best way: the Ember Toss (tech 11, next room) flies
# through a 32 tall gap (the ember is a point 22 u above the floor) and teleports the player
# beyond it, so one toss skips one gap. There are two gaps in a row and the toss has a 12 s
# cooldown, so a toss cannot skip both; the player needs a crouch-dash for the other, or to wait
# 720 frames for a second toss. A crouch-dash has a 24 frame cooldown and risks nothing; a toss
# thrown from B's face ends at x 1350, over the pit, and the player arrives in it (tests/replay/
# zone1/10_*_toss_*). About 3 s for a skilled player (the teaching route crosses at frame 178).
room zone1/10_crouch_dash_under
size 60 34
spawn 74 960
tiles
